# Pressing Space on a checkbox must say what it became.
#
# Reported on hardware: "checkboxes are not announced when they are checked or
# unchecked." Two causes, both real.
#
# First, Space is a typing keystroke, so TypingState suppressed the toggle's
# ValueChanged as though it were an edit re-reading its own growing value. That
# gate now applies only to controls the user types INTO — a checkbox's value
# does not grow as you type, it changes because you asked it to, which is
# exactly what has to be heard.
#
# Second, there was no rule for it. The role rules match a ValueChanged too and
# would have re-announced the whole control, so these win on priority and say
# only what changed.

node off Checkbox "Speak typed characters"
node on  Checkbox "Speak typed characters" states=Checked
focus off
drain
changed on
drain
changed off

expect
  Speak typed characters, check box, not checked
  checked
  not checked
